        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Are walking pads cheaper on Black Friday?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sometimes, but less often than the badges suggest. Walking pads are discounted for much of the year, so a Black Friday price may be the same as the September price. On 28 October 2026 all six pads on our watch list were already selling below their "compare at" prices. Compare any Black Friday price with what the pad sold for in October, not with its list price.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is a good Black Friday price for a walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One meaningfully below what that pad has been selling for in recent weeks. We use roughly 10 to 15% below the October selling price as our threshold, which gives targets such as $269 for the WalkingPad Z1 and $219 for the UREVO SpaceWalk 3S. Those are our judgements, not predictions of what sellers will charge.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>When do walking pad Black Friday deals start?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Black Friday 2026 is Friday 27 November. Amazon had not announced its 2026 event dates when we checked on 28 October, but its Black Friday week typically starts about a week before Thanksgiving, and many prices that fall early stay down through Cyber Monday on 30 November. Brand stores often run their own promotions earlier.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is it better to buy a walking pad from Amazon or the brand’s own store?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Check both. WalkingPad, UREVO and MERACH all sell direct, and the prices often differ. In October the UREVO Strol 2E was cheaper on UREVO's store than on the Amazon listings we saw, while the WalkingPad Z1 was the same price on both. On Amazon, make sure the seller is the brand or Amazon so the warranty applies.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Should I buy a Sperax walking pad on sale?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. On 16 April 2026 the CPSC told consumers to stop using Sperax walking pads and treadmills immediately, citing sudden speed changes and stops that caused falls, and reports of overheating and fires. The importer refused an acceptable recall. The CPSC asks owners not to resell them, so avoid second-hand units too.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does a higher horsepower walking pad mean a better deal?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Walking pad horsepower figures are usually peak ratings used for marketing, and independent sources often put the continuous rating far lower; on the WalkingPad Z1 the figures range from 2.25 HP to 0.75 HP. Compare belt length, speed range, weight capacity and warranty instead.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

